{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305132,"nonce":"fkDrrO4nKJ2pElURHP77w3++b20=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPhiWg","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/14","origin":"github"},"title":"--minsize defaults to 1 MiB, so small files are never recoverable","message":"```python\nMINIMUM_FILESIZE_TO_SEARCH = 1024 * 1024\n...\nreturn [fi[\"length\"] for fi in info[\"files\"] if fi[\"length\"] \u003e int(args.minsize)]\n```\n\nFiles at or below 1 MiB are excluded from the set of sizes searched for on disk, so `file_length in files` is always false for them and they are silently skipped.\n\nFor a torrent made mostly of small files the tool recovers nothing at all by default, without saying why.\n\nThe default should be 0. Filtering small files is a performance heuristic that belongs behind an explicit opt-in, not a silent default that changes what can be recovered.","files":null}]}